    Guard the Necromancer lit-square penalty against a stale position
    
    Patch 0099 tests square_islit(cave, borg.c) to apply the game's
    lit-square penalty.  borg.c is refreshed by the map update, so on the
    first think after changing levels it still holds the previous level's
    position; on a smaller level that position lies outside the new
    chunk's square array and square_islit reads outside it (its bounds
    assert is compiled out in the product; borg-rs#21 recorded SIGSEGV in
    every Necromancer game at the first return to town).  Treat an
    out-of-bounds recorded position as unlit.
    
    Fixture: necrolight-296-crash (stale-town at the recorded geometry,
    stale-far deterministic anchor, lit/dark/mage-lit in-bounds controls);
    added to the regression matrix as the necrolight-crash group.

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-magic.c b/src/borg/borg-magic.c
index 9598d0a48..963cd245a 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-magic.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-magic.c
@@ -530,8 +530,12 @@ int borg_spell_fail_rate(const enum borg_spells spell)
     }
 
     /* Necromancers are punished by being on lit squares, whatever lights
-     * them (their own light, permanent light, a monster's light) */
+     * them (their own light, permanent light, a monster's light).  The
+     * recorded position can predate the map update of a freshly entered,
+     * smaller level and lie outside its bounds; treat such a square as
+     * unlit instead of reading outside the array. */
     if (borg.trait[BI_CLASS] == CLASS_NECROMANCER &&
+        square_in_bounds(cave, borg.c) &&
         square_islit(cave, borg.c)) {
         chance += 25;
 
